# The live session behaves like an installed one: both accounts carry the
# password "live", and sudo asks for it -- in a terminal, in the polkit
# agent, and in the root gate's approval window. The live user is not in
# wheel, so the rule is explicit: passworded, all commands, no exceptions.
live ALL=(ALL) ALL
# No sudo lecture for the live user: the gate's `sudo -S` (no tty, the
# password on a pipe) meets the first-time lecture badly -- the read dies
# with exit 1 and the installer never starts. The lecture is a nicety the
# live session can do without.
Defaults:live lecture=never
